<p>
As I do every year on this day, I want to wish Happy Birthday to <i>Dark Side of the Moon</i>, the best album of all time by the best rock band of all time, Pink Floyd. Of course, you&rsquo;re free to disagree. I absolutely support your right to be wrong.
</p>
<p>
I used to feature a track from Dark Side of the Moon with each yearly post but I&rsquo;ve run out of songs from that album so I&rsquo;ve moved on to tracks from other Albums that I really like. This year&rsquo;s track is <i>Lost for Words</i> from a rehearsal for the Pulse tour. If the video doesn&rsquo;t appear on your screen, click on &ldquo;Watch video on YouTube&rdquo;.
</p>
<p>
I like this video for two reasons. First, you don&rsquo;t usually see Gilmour playing a straight guitar but he brings the same amazing technique to it that he uses on his electric guitar. Second, these guys don&rsquo;t mess around. Even though it&rsquo;s a rehearsal for a song they&rsquo;ve probably played hundreds of times, they treat it just like a live show complete with their signature light show.
</p>
